Z||000000||RobertVol||10-30-2001||01:36 PM||||A while back I had asked about clutches and I was given some good answers.<P>I was going to go with George@the Fieroshop. <P>Yes I remember the thread but I make my own judgments and think it is a quality part. <P>BUT! the price is a little high....<P>I will not replace this clutch myself,I wont take that chance if something goes wrong. So thats why price is an issue...7.5 hours of labor adds up!..LMAO<P><BR>I need to know the best for the price...<P>lets see...<P>Centerforce<BR>Borg Warner<BR>Luk<BR>RAM....<P>Pleas give plusses and minuses on above mentioned<P>Please suggest one.. I would purchase the Fieroshops but over 400.00 dollars for a clutch of any type is a little high for me. <P>I drive my car hard but its only a lightly modified 2.8. I dont think I need that clamp load.. <P>But you never know <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks in advance..<P>I havent been on the board in awhile...CLIFF it looks good <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P><A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RobsGT2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||10-30-2001||01:49 PM||||I hope you have better luck than I did asking the same information recently.<P>If you do a search on 'Clutch' here, about 90% of the replies you get are threads in which people tell you to use the search function when asking about clutches. The other 10% of the replies that come up have lots of opinions, but no consensus whatsoever. <P>I'm looking for *the* clutch for a 2.8 as well. So far, I have no idea what I'll be spending my money on. <P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||10-30-2001||02:01 PM||||Same here.  All my searches did was turn up posts telling me to do a search.  And a smattering of "this clutch is best" posts, but rarely would two people agree.  <P>I'm leaning heavily towards the Centerforce that Archie sells for his V8 swaps (assuming it'll work on a 2.8) next time around.  LZeitgeist and I put a Ram HD (not Racing) clutch in my Formula last Winter.  20,000 miles later it still seems ok.  I could chirp 2nd on a quick shift when it was new, but can't do that anymore.  Overall, I'm satisfied with the RAM on a totally stock 2.8, but I'm not confident it would hold up on a modded engine.  If I had it to do over, I'd probably try the RAM Racing Clutch or Archie's Centerforce.  <P>BTW, the RAM HD clutch feels just like a stock clutch in driving.  It's just supposed to have about 30% more grip.  Can't say cuz my OEM clutch was bad when I bought the car.||||reg||6
