Z||000007||Fierowrecker||10-30-2001||05:31 PM||||Hey Bob!<BR>Just about any NAME BRAND clutch will work...<BR>IF you have the flywheel resurfaced...<BR>Otherwise, buy the cheapest clutch, and stick it in...<BR>I bought the cheapest, did NOT resurface the flywheel, and first and second gears will slip...<BR>But that is with a tranny and engine package that is going to be replaced...<BR>The next clutch will be quality, along with a resurfaced flywheel, but that will be on a 3800 and a better tranny...<BR>Just remember, some of those clutches are NOT meant for the street, but for 1/4 mile blasts...<BR>Check the specs of the clutch...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroPerformance||10-30-2001||05:46 PM||||I bought a Borg Warner heavy duty clutch for my GT's isuzu transmission. I think it was about $130 and the guy that I bought it from said that he used it on a 500hp car he used to drag race.<P>-Charlie||||reg||1
