Z||000010||Archie||10-30-2001||08:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RobertVol:<BR><B>Archie - <P>Any cost reduction to purchase from you the centerforce??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> heh heh <P>I am thinking of going with the Centerforce...<P>Thanks for all the opinions...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You know, that's a good idea.<P>CenterForce sells the DF201914 clutch for 362.95 according to their Web Site, that is the best clutch C-Force offers to the public. <P>The clutch that I have C-Force making for me is called the Ball-Bearing clutch and has 20% more clamping power.  Normally my clutch sells seperately for $375.00, I have 10 of them in stock and for this week, I'll sell them for 325.00 ea. This Ball Bearing clutch is the newest thing I have C-Force making up for me. <P>Ok, that good enough?<P>Archie ||||reg||1
Z||000011||RobertVol||10-30-2001||08:37 PM||||Hmmm Archie you drive a HARD bargain <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sounds like a plan though....<BR>What else will I need with that?<P>Explain in laymans terms..I love Fieros but other than Air and Oil Filter changes I stay out of the Mechanics Field.. heh heh<P>The reson I ask Is I want to over haul this whole clutch assembly.. What else at the time I replace..? <P>BTW.. You will be receiving e mail on this deal! <P>Let me just pay off of my balance on my VISA <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> this week ...<P>You can accept Visa right&gt; ? Pay pal? Let me know and thanks||||reg||1
Z||000012||Archie||10-30-2001||09:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RobertVol:<BR><B>Hmmm Archie you drive a HARD bargain  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sounds like a plan though....<BR>What else will I need with that?<P>You can accept Visa right&gt; ? Pay pal? Let me know and thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You just need the correct T.O.B. for the transmission you have.<P>Yeah, I take Visa, MC & Discover..... PayPal is for those that don't take credit cards.<P>Anyone else want a deal on a clutch?<P>Archie<BR><P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
Z||000013||GT GT 87||10-30-2001||09:16 PM||||Hey Archie ........I see at Jeg's , they have a CF # ms361914 and a dual friction  #201914 for 289$ , the df has no take up springs in the disc . and looks metalic. What is dual friction ?  Steve||||reg||1
Z||000014||skitime||10-30-2001||09:29 PM||||Hey Archie,  Sent a PM||||reg||1
Z||000015||Archie||10-31-2001||12:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GT GT 87:<BR><B>Hey Archie ........I see at Jeg's , they have a CF # ms361914 and a dual friction  #201914 for 289$ , the df has no take up springs in the disc . and looks metalic. What is dual friction ?  Steve</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>According to their web site the MS part numbers are just plain jane clutches with organic materials on both sides. The DF numbers are Dual Friction which has organic material on one side and metalic on the other side. I don't know what you mean by "take up springs", if you mean the springs in the center hub, I can tell you for sure that all CForce DF clutches that we've been talking about in this thread do in fact have the hub springs.<P>I don't have a Jeg's catalog handy here but I'll look at it tomorrow.<P>Archie ||||reg||1
